 "case:locations.hall.art.props.6.label": "Front door",
 "case:locations.hall.description": "A baronial hall of dark panelling and antlers, with a stage for the band and a fireplace you could stand up in, still smoking this morning. Through an arch is the bar, its four hundred whiskies on shelves to the ceiling. Reception is by the front door, with the night porter’s desk and the board of brass room keys behind it.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_bar.label": "The bar",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_bar.text": "Tomasz is polishing glasses that don’t need it. Behind him, in a cardboard box, are the supper’s red table candles in their tartan holders.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_fire.label": "The fireplace",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_fire.text": "When the lights went out, Mr Munro set candles in the hotel’s silver sticks along this mantelpiece, and Dame Vivienne stood here and sang ‘My Love Is Like a Red, Red Rose’ to thirty frightened people. White wax has run down the stone.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_reception.label": "Reception",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_reception.text": "The night book lies open on the desk. Mr Munro shows you the note he made this morning when he rang the gritting depot.",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_stage.label": "The stage",
 "case:locations.hall.hotspots.hs_gh_stage.text": "The band’s instruments are still in their cases; nobody can leave the glen. Their leader, Ewan, shows you his camera.",
 "case:locations.hall.name": "The Great Hall",
 "case:locations.hall.summary": "The stage, the bar, reception and the great fireplace.",
